    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36377" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνυβρ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>insult</i> or <i>mock</i> one <i>in</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					342
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ ἐν κακοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					68
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήμου ἐνυβρίξῃς ἁγνὸν τάφον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					195
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Vaxos</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. dat. pers., <i>insult,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναιξίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					10.26.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				237 vi 17
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴς τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					34.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> abs., <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				720
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> in 
				Pass.
			, Medic., of ulcers, <i>to be irritated,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.120
			</span></i>.</div>
